<metadata><name>Mount Thielsen Trail</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:303-3: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.146104" lon="-122.127560"><ele>1649.2</ele><name>Thielsen Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 550916942 Mount Thielsen Trailhead parking); confidence: high; pdf_page: 305; book_elev_ft: 5320; quote: The trailhead is at Thielsen Sno-Park on Highway 138, 2.7 miles south of the Diamond Lake Resort access road.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.156672" lon="-122.106865"><ele>1901.6</ele><name>Spruce Ridge Trail junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 5320603737, Mount Thielsen Trail x Spruce Ridge Trail; confidence: high; pdf_page: 305; quote: From the sno-park the trail climbs moderately, then more steeply, 1.5 miles to the Spruce Ridge Trail.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.153536" lon="-122.080762"><ele>2235.0</ele><name>End of the Mount Thielsen Trail (PCT junction)</name><desc>source: OSM node 980043658, Mount Thielsen Trail x Pacific Crest Trail; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 305; book_elev_ft: 7320; quote: The end of this trail, 3.7 miles from the sno-park, takes you to 7,320 feet, a climb of 2,000 feet</desc></wpt>
